{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>ואם.</b> The word מאן is a demonstrative, like ושבח אני את המתים (Ecclesiastes 4:2), and the meaning of נגף is like משחית, and so it is written וצפרדע ותשחיתם (Psalms 78:45). The commentators disagreed concerning the word צפרדעים: many said it is a species of fish found in Egypt, called in Arabic al-timsāḥ, which comes out of the river and seizes people; and others said they are those found in river channels that make a sound, and this is the correct one in my eyes, and it is the well-known one."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's lemma is ואם (corresponding to the beginning of Exodus 7:27 in some traditions, = 8:1 in English numbering); the plague verse discussion concerns the frog plague. The identification of al-timsāḥ with the crocodile is well known but left untranslated per instructions."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:31.503708217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}